        "title": "Fungal Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nECTOMYCORRHIZAL (ECM) FUNGI:\n  Form a sheath (mantle) around the root tip\n  Hyphae grow between root cortex cells (Hartig net) but NOT inside cells\n  Hyphal network extends into soil → enormous surface area"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-ECOLOGY.md#021",
      "path": [
        "03-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:mycology:03-ecology, git-history:mycology:03-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fungal Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PARTNERS:\n  Fungi: ~20,000 ECM species; Basidiomycetes dominant (Amanita, Boletus,\n    Cantharellus, Suillus, Lactarius, Cortinarius, Russula)\n    + some Ascomycetes (Tuber/truffle, Elaphomyces)\n  Plants: ~8,000 species; mostly trees: Pinus, Quercus, Betula, Fagus,\n    Eucalyptus, Larix, Populus\n  → ECM trees dominate most temperate and boreal forests"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-ECOLOGY.md#022",
      "path": [
        "03-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:mycology:03-ecology, git-history:mycology:03-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fungal Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXCHANGE:\n  Plant → Fungus: sucrose (sugar, the photosynthate)\n  Fungus → Plant: Pi (inorganic phosphorus), N (as amino acids), water\n  Rate: plant allocates 10–20% of net primary production to ECM\n  Fungus provides: what the plant can't reach with just roots\n    → Fungal hyphae: 1–10 µm; root hairs: 10–20 µm; roots: much larger\n    → Hyphae access micropores in soil that roots cannot penetrate"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-ECOLOGY.md#023",
      "path": [
        "03-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:mycology:03-ecology, git-history:mycology:03-ecology]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[ecology]",
        "current_path": "mycology/03-ECOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:ecology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ecology]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fungal Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SPECIFICITY:\n  Not random: specific plant-fungal pairings, though not absolute\n  Suillus: specific to Pinus; Rhizopogon: specific to some Pinus/Pseudotsuga\n  Amanita muscaria: wide host range (many tree genera)\n  Truffle (Tuber melanosporum): specific to Quercus, Corylus in wild\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-ECOLOGY.md#024",
      "path": [
        "03-ECOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
